## What the campaign has established

The reviewed census-coverage theorem supplies necessary conditions for
normalized minimal counterexamples at arbitrary degree. The enumerated
window is still finite: at n <= 200 the accepted chain is 24,063 census rows
-> 90 actual-stabilizer rows -> 64 residual necessary configurations.
Those 64 consist of 44 u_s = 1 rows and 20 u_s >= 2 rows. They are not
polynomial pairs. See `AUDIT.md`, 17(ccccccccc), 17(ggggggggggg), and the
dated 2026-09-06T04:03Z state.

Internal (99,66) and D=108 computations remain undecided; earlier internal
closure announcements were superseded by support/radius/stratum corrections.
But the external GGHV degree99 exclusion now puts new99 frontier work on HOLD
pending its primary-source applicability gate (see below). These are different
evidence layers, not competing definitions of an open mathematical problem.
The K16 theorem (T) is promoted only for t <= 8. Neither this finite range
nor excluding the whole K16 ray would by itself resolve plane JC2.

## Current proof fronts

| Front | Accepted reduction / useful object | Remaining obligation |
|---|---|---|
| u_s = 1 receivers | Licensed Moh descent, with the child's own characteristic data and full source support | Exclude the necessary polynomial receivers uniformly, or find a structural descent that strictly improves an invariant. The 44 rows are only the n <= 200 test population. |
| Split branches | Corrected two-point systems; characteristic-degree attainment; direct T2+T3 compression under review | Prove the source-to-chart implication, then decide the full necessary system. The 20 class-C rows, (99,66) split branches, and D=108 are clients, not an all-degree finite classification. |
| K16 prototype | Whole-polynomial equation (UF), reconstructed ideals K_m, and the terminal target B*eta | A uniform argument on the required nonzero-product locus, plus the separate b = 0 boundary. All coefficient-field factors and actual degrees must be covered. |

The general proof needs exclusion of every datum supplied by the coverage
theorem, without an unproved degree, support, depth, or height cap. A source
row sharing numerical parameters with a solved receiver does not inherit its
certificate without a proved map. Keep an explicit unassigned branch when a
receiver map has not been established.

### Counterexample front: full-ideal properness

The completed [different-model gate](xmodel/full-ideal-counterexample-gate-fable5-20260906.md)
confirms that every point of the COMPLETE direct ideal reconstructs polynomials
of degrees (99,66) or (108,72) with nonzero constant Jacobian. The one-way
implication is promoted with the corrections in `AUDIT.md` 17(ppppppppppp).
Exact properness would give a counterexample by Nullstellensatz and
plane-automorphism degree divisibility; explicit coordinates or a canonical
resultant lift would not be logically required. NO PROPERNESS IS KNOWN.

This does not apply to the live 466-row proper-subset solve, modular points,
or truncated survivors. The frozen full builder has a completion-count
assertion bug; its executable output needs separate repair/validation.
The gate's suggestion to discard `t3eq` as rowless is wrong and is not
adopted. A subset unit excludes the full chart; excluding a source
configuration still needs the unproved source-to-chart interface.

The [nonemptiness pilot](xmodel/nonemptiness-certificate-astra-20260906.md)
specifies a smaller acceptance certificate: exact coordinates in a nonzero
finite Q-algebra, checked against every full row through the circuit. It
has no candidate. A smooth mod-p subsystem alone does not certify a lift.
The recovered all-degree characteristic-tower analogue is now independently
reviewed, with exact hypotheses in AUDIT 17(sssssssssss). It is recovery of
an old appendix, not an existence or exclusion result. The review's proposed
T3 replacement is not automatically equivalent on every D108 T2 chart, nor
