### K16: use the conclusion the terminal chart consumes

The current U_eta proposal asks for eta_m = 0 on V(K_m) with b != 0.
The recorded implication chain actually consumes B_m*eta_m = 0 there.
Consequently a sufficient, weaker open-chart target is

```text
For every actual m >= 4 and every factor of Q[d]/(3d^2-m),
V(K_m) has no geometric point with b*B_m*eta_m != 0.
```

This is a coordinator target selection, not a new exclusion theorem.
It follows from the existing specialization/terminal-target chain in
[the whole-polynomial report](xmodel/k16-ueta-classification-astra-20260906.md),
section 8. The product target itself was already explicit in
[the earlier Abel report](xmodel/k16-f3abel-astra-20260905.md); this restores
that target rather than claiming a new mathematical mechanism.

The same report's SUPPORT argument says B != 0 forces support gcd 1.
Thus the B = 0 parity families need no exclusion for this product target.
The b = 0 boundary remains an independent obligation. Full classification
of all polynomial solutions is stronger than the conclusion currently needed.
THICK rules out a fixed nilpotence exponent; it does not rule out a proved
formula whose exponent grows with the parameter.

The [reviewed boundary lemma](xmodel/k16-boundary-product-gate-fable5-20260906.md)
now returns marked rational solutions to polynomials when B!=0, and an exact
